cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use gp3sequences in your work, please cite the software using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "gp3sequences: Transparent Analysis of Ordered Categorical Sequences"
version: "0.2.0.9000"
license: "MIT"
abstract: >-
  gp3sequences provides transparent, reproducible, and auditable tools for
  validating, preparing, encoding, summarising, comparing, modelling, and
  diagnosing ordered categorical sequence data. It supports explicit
  preprocessing policies, motifs and bounded subsequences, consensus and
  group comparisons, sequence distances and clustering, transition networks,
  higher-order models, categorical hidden Markov models, longitudinal and
  time-varying workflows, design-aware inference, provenance contracts,
  visual diagnostics, and guarded interoperability with specialist packages.
identifiers:
